# framing.local.md — per-FOB sensitive values (LOCAL ONLY)

> **This file (when copied to `framing.local.md`) is gitignored.**
> Do not commit it. Do not share its contents. Treat the values here
> the same way you treat your physical FOB.

Copy this file to `framing.local.md` (drop the `.example`) before
working through SDR steps 06 and 07.

## FOB-specific values
_filled in after step 06_

- **Serial** (28 bits): `0x_______`
- **Function codes**:
  - Start:  `0x_`
  - Lock:   `0x_`
  - Unlock: `0x_`
  - Trunk:  `0x_`

## Captured hopping codes
_populate as you extract from URH; used as inputs to `validate-key.py`_

| Capture file              | Button | Hopping (hex) | Counter (decrypted) | Function (decrypted) |
|---------------------------|--------|---------------|---------------------|----------------------|
| fob-start-001.bits        | Start  | 0x________    |                     |                      |
| fob-start-002.bits        | Start  | 0x________    |                     |                      |
| fob-start-003.bits        | Start  | 0x________    |                     |                      |
| fob-lock-001.bits         | Lock   | 0x________    |                     |                      |
| fob-unlock-001.bits       | Unlock | 0x________    |                     |                      |

## Device key recovery
_filled in after step 07; **NEVER put the actual key here either**_

- Path used: A (Flipper DB) / B (PICkit) / C (cryptanalytic)
- Date recovered: YYYY-MM-DD
- Validation result: counter increments by 1 across N consecutive captures? yes / no
- Device key lives in: `esp32/src/secrets.py` (gitignored)

## Backup plan

If you lose `framing.local.md` you can re-derive everything by re-running
the SDR walkthrough. If you lose `esp32/src/secrets.py` (which has the
recovered device key) the same applies. Consider a one-line note in a
password manager like:

    vroom-spectra-fob:
      serial: 0x_______
      key:    0x_______________
      counter (as of YYYY-MM-DD): _____

…stored encrypted at rest. Not in plain text.
